What each one should contain
1. SharePoint Site URL

This should be the full site URL, not just the host.

Use:

https://wincowindow.sharepoint.com/sites/CRMDocuments

This replaces:

varSiteUrl = "https://wincowindow.sharepoint.com/sites/CRMDocuments"
2. SharePoint Library Name

This should be the exact SharePoint library name used by the connector.

Use:

Opportunity

This replaces:

varLibraryName = "Opportunity"
3. SharePoint Parent Folder Name

Only keep this as an environment variable if you actually use it in logic. Right now your flow initializes:

varParentFolder = "Opportunity"

But in the JSON you shared, it is not doing much useful work. If your path is simply:

/Opportunity/<TargetFolderName>

then this variable may be unnecessary.

If you keep it, value would be:

Opportunity
4. Parent SharePoint Document Location ID

This is the big one for deployment.

Right now you hardcoded:

/sharepointdocumentlocations(cbeb6f18-c321-f111-8341-002248081a6f)

That GUID will almost certainly be different in Dev, Test, and Prod.

So the environment variable value should be just the GUID:

cbeb6f18-c321-f111-8341-002248081a6f

Then the bind should be built dynamically.

5. Duplicate Handling Mode

Right now your flow initializes:

varDuplicateMode = "ctp_DuplicateMode"

That is just the literal text ctp_DuplicateMode, not the actual mode.

This variable should hold the real behavior value, such as:

rename

or

fail

For your solution, I would recommend:

fail

unless the business explicitly wants same-name files preserved automatically.

